      "side": 1,
      "message": "A RenderStep that advertises `kInverseFillsScissor` is required to just render a pixel-aligned rect matching `params.scissor()`. Given that, my expectation would be that any sort of numerically unstable transform would manifest as errors in the computed local coordinates, but not in the fragment coords that are touched.\n\nDid Agent Smith find a way to still exploit this?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 91,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 91,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "08ffb5c559c1f21314c9302c3c01da96ad8d3de7",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5f23f89b_0e6565b3",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/Renderer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 122,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-11T23:20:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we are scissoring every dst-reading draw to its own draw bounds, we\u0027ll be thrashing the scissor state.  If we pass in the aggregate dst read bounds that will be used for the texture copy (which I think we know at this point since DrawList accumulates it before snapping, right?), then we just have to return the intersection of that and `params.scissor()` and not worry about rounding out the `drawBounds`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 122,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 122,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "08ffb5c559c1f21314c9302c3c01da96ad8d3de7",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
