      "lineNbr": 126,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-11T23:20:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "returning nullopt means don\u0027t change the scissor, shouldn\u0027t we want to return an empty scissor rect to disable rendering entirely?\n\nFor that matter, it is a little unexpected that we\u0027d both encounter a `drawBounds` that was empty or inverted (but I can\u0027t rule out we didn\u0027t get here from the update to drawBounds for `kIgnoreInverseFill` above).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 126,
        "startChar": 49,
        "endLine": 126,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "08ffb5c559c1f21314c9302c3c01da96ad8d3de7",
